From 277dc1f63299b2067d6fabad05cad7dc7266b029 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 11:22:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Offer a confirmed reset when startup lock settings are
 unreadable (#87)

security-store.cjs now classifies read failures: SECURITY_UNAVAILABLE
when Windows credential protection is unavailable, SECURITY_UNREADABLE
when the file cannot be decrypted, is oversized or is not valid JSON.
Security.load records the reason; invalid settings structure also
counts as unreadable, other file-system errors do not.

When protection is available but the settings are unreadable, the lock
screen offers "Reset lock settings..." with the consequences stated and
a typed RESET confirmation. Reset renames the file to
security-settings.bin.<time>.unreadable (never deleted), starts with the
lock off and logs the backup name in the main process. Reset is never
offered for readable settings, a wrong password, unavailable protection
or other I/O errors, and there is no plaintext fallback.

Adds unit tests for classification, quarantine and refusal cases and
security-lock.browser.test.cjs (stubbed bridge) to test:browser.
Physical Windows DPAPI behaviour is not verified.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
